{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who</b> — I would wonder: who will lead me to the city of Edom, which was under siege. And I myself would answer my soul: HaShem will do this, who guided me to Edom. But now my thought has turned about, because of \"Have not You, Elohim, forsaken us?\" The meaning: what will our armies do if You do not go out with them?"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:22.838299026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}